It is Thursday morning.
I sit with Vikram in the office.
Vikram is the tester for our software project.
"I have worked here for five years," Vikram says.
"I have tested many applications thoroughly."
I listen carefully about his experience.
After that, he looks at my computer.
"Maya, I have prepared a testing plan for your code," he says.
He opens a file.
"Have you written the new code?" he asks me.
"Yes, I have written the first part," I tell him.
Vikram explains all the points of his plan.
I have understood his explanation completely.
His careful work is very useful for our project.
Now I do the next work with confidence.
